\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The trace criterion for tuples}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{\citet{v1, §3.2, Corollary 2, p. 9, and §1, (2), p. 2}{futorny2017specht}
recover Wiegmann's simultaneous unitary similarity criterion
for tuples of square complex matrices from their criterion
for systems of maps. It compares traces of words in tuple
entries and their adjoints. For the two Hermitian operators
of \ref{fdip-018Y}, taking adjoints leaves both letters
unchanged. The specialization compares one tuple with its
complex conjugate. Its finite length bound comes from the
simultaneous block span of \ref{fdip-018U}.}

\p{In the same source, §1, (1), p. 2 gives Specht's
single-matrix criterion with the matrix and its adjoint,
and the discussion of Pearcy's finite check on p. 3 concerns
that single-matrix setting.}
